---
description: Always surface user-facing action feedback with SweetAlert2 (toast or modal) via flash() or inline Swal.
alwaysApply: true
---

# SweetAlert Notifications (Global)

Whenever the user performs **any** meaningful action across the application (create, send, update, delete, archive, upload, etc.), show an elegant **SweetAlert2** toast or modal.

## Preferred pattern (server redirects)

Use the app helper so layouts can render the alert from session flash:

```php
flash()->success('تم الحفظ بنجاح.');
flash()->info('تم أرشفة العنصر.');
flash()->warning('تحقق من البيانات.');
flash()->error('تعذّر إكمال العملية.');
```

Layouts (`layouts/admin`, `layouts/marketing`, etc.) must load SweetAlert2 and fire `Swal.fire` when `session('flasher')` is present.

## AJAX / destructive confirms

For in-page AJAX (e.g. soft delete), use SweetAlert confirmation first, then a success/error toast after the request:

```js
Swal.fire({ icon: 'warning', showCancelButton: true, /* ... */ })
  .then(/* fetch … then toast */);
```

## Do not

- Rely only on silent redirects or plain HTML banners for primary success/error feedback when SweetAlert is available.
- Skip confirmation for destructive deletes when the product UX expects it.
